"fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "EDITOR", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{'headers':['Col1'],'rows':[{'col1':'row1'},{'col1':'row2'}, {'col1':'row3'}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": null, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": "<p>Cooking is great fun for children, but remember to talk to them about how to stay safe in the kitchen.   Adults should always supervise children when cooking.</p>\n<p>Safety rules might include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Always ask an adult before you cook.</li>\n<li>Ask an adult if you need boiling water or a hot oven.</li>\n<li>Ask an adult to supervise when you use a knife.</li>\n<li>Move carefully in the kitchen - don't run around.</li>\n<li>Wipe up any spills straight away so noone slips.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<p>Hygiene rules might include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wash your hands with soap and water.</li>\n<li>Wipe down work surfaces before you start.</li>\n<li>Tie back long hair and wear and apron if you have one.</li>\n<li>If you lick your fingers, wash your hands again.</li>\n<li>Keep cooked and uncooked food separate. Be especially careful with raw meat and fish.</li>\n<li>Ask an adult to check everything is properly cooked before you eat it.</li>\n</ul>\n", "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": false, "selectedModalId": 0, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}], "details": {"id": 219, "name": "Kitchen Safety", "logCreatedAt": "2023-06-20T14:10:02.751387", "logUpdatedAt": "2023-06-20T14:10:02.751387", "logCreatedById": 108180408, "logUpdatedById": 108180408, "nameForContentDev": null}}, "order": 4, "btnType": "SECONDARY", "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileNam